  "issue": {
    "body": "I would like to be able to raise `HTTPException` with custom headers.\r\n\r\nI'm willing to implement it and send a PR if this is something acceptable for Starlette.\r\n\r\nCurrently, that's not possible. As the headers would have to be set in an exception handler, and it wouldn't have a way to know the associated realms of a specific exception raised.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nUse case:\r\n\r\nI would like to be able to raise an authentication error 401 Unauthorized, including `WWW-Authenticate`, with a specific type (like `Basic`) and possibly, with a specific set of realms.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? Would that be acceptable/desirable in Starlette?",
    "closed_at": "2019-01-04T14:41:27Z",
    "created_at": "2018-12-28T16:23:38Z",
